#
# prototype -- GNU patch 2.5.9's installed layout.
#
# AUTHORED, NOT GENERATED, and carrying no host paths: build.sh runs
# `pkgmk -r <destroot>`, which resolves each path below against the staged
# tree.  pkgproto could not have produced this file anyway -- it silently omits
# symlinks, and the symlink is the line that makes the package usable.
#
# NO INSTALL SCRIPTS.  CLASSES=none, class `none` on every object.  SVR4
# install scripts have never been run on Amix under its 1992 pre-POSIX
# /bin/sh, so this is a pure file payload (D9).
#
i pkginfo
#
# --- the program ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# /usr/local exists on a stock Amix root (dated Nov 1991, with an empty bin/),
# and it is this repo's shared prefix.  It is declared rather than assumed:
# SVR4's contents DB handles a directory owned by more than one package, and a
# package that silently depends on a directory it did not declare is a package
# that fails on the one box where somebody removed it.
d none /usr/local 0755 root sys
d none /usr/local/bin 0755 root sys
f none /usr/local/bin/patch 0755 root bin
#
# ★ THE SYMLINK, AND WHY ITS TARGET IS ABSOLUTE
#
# It is belt-and-braces rather than load-bearing: measured on the box, the stock
# Amix PATH already begins with /usr/local/bin --
#
#   PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/ccs/bin:/sbin:/usr/sbin:/etc:/usr/ucb:
#        /usr/amiga/bin:/usr/public/bin:/usr/hosts
#
# -- so `patch` resolves to ours without any link at all, and ahead of the
# Larry Wall patch 12u4 that the stock `public` package puts in
# /usr/public/bin.  The link exists for a root whose PATH has been trimmed.
#
# ★ THE TARGET IS ABSOLUTE BECAUSE STOCK pkgadd CORRUPTS A RELATIVE ONE.
#
# Measured on the golden 030 box, same .pkg, same admin file, both engines:
#
#   stock    /usr/sbin/pkgadd   -> /usr/bin/patch -> /../local/bin/patch  DANGLING
#   heirloom /usr/apkg/bin/pkgadd -> /usr/bin/patch -> ../local/bin/patch  correct
#
# The pkgmap line was byte-identical in both runs (`s none
# /usr/bin/patch=../local/bin/patch`), so this is an ENGINE defect, not a
# packaging one: stock pkgadd prepends the install root to a relative symlink
# target.  It reports "Installation was successful" either way -- the link just
# does not resolve, and /../local/bin/patch is a path that cannot exist.
#
# The package manager's own APKG ships `s none /usr/bin/apkg=../apkg/bin/apkg`
# and is fine on this box because it was installed by the heirloom engine.  A
# package this repo ships must work on a BARE box, where the only engine is the
# stock one -- so the relative form is not available to us.
#
# The cost is alt-root correctness: an absolute target is wrong under
# `pkgadd -R`.  That is the right trade here.  Nobody alt-root-installs a
# developer tool, whereas a dangling /usr/bin/patch on a stock box is a real,
# silent failure -- and stock `core` itself uses absolute targets for exactly
# this reason (`s none /usr/bin/uname=/sbin/uname`).
#
# An `s` line carries NO mode/owner/group -- that is the pkgmap(4) grammar for
# a symlink.  /usr/bin is NOT re-declared: it exists and belongs to `core`, so
# this adds exactly one contents record and touches no core-owned object.
s none /usr/bin/patch=/usr/local/bin/patch
#
# --- manual page ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Under the package's own prefix, not /usr/share/man: writing into the stock
# man tree would put our file inside a directory the `man` package owns, and
# the parallel-prefix rule this family follows exists to keep stock and
# add-on trees separable.  Add /usr/local/man to MANPATH to read it.
d none /opt 0755 root sys
d none /opt/amix 0755 root sys
d none /opt/amix/man 0755 root sys
d none /opt/amix/man/1 0755 root sys
f none /opt/amix/man/1/patch 0644 root bin
d none /opt/amix/man/whatis.d 0755 root sys
f none /opt/amix/man/whatis.d/patch 0644 root bin
#
# --- licence and upstream notes ---------------------------------------------
#
# GPL-2.0-or-later: the licence text travels with the binary, which is both the
# licence's requirement and this repo's rule.
d none /usr/local/doc 0755 root sys
d none /usr/local/doc/patch 0755 root sys
f none /usr/local/doc/patch/COPYING 0644 root bin
f none /usr/local/doc/patch/NEWS 0644 root bin
f none /usr/local/doc/patch/README 0644 root bin
